  "_mapping_notes": {
    "sld_node_type": "Populated \u2014 maps each Revit family/type to the corresponding node_type in sld_system_model.md Symbol Registry (e.g., 'L2-1', 'A-3'). 'TBD' indicates items needing a new SLD node type. null indicates no applicable mapping.",
    "sld_node_variant": "Optional per-entry variant discriminator. When present, the entry is keyed (sld_node_type, sld_node_variant) in the resolver's variant dictionary instead of the node-type dictionary, letting one node type map to several families/types (e.g. L2-7 spare vs. space). The two L2-7 entries (spare/space) carry variants; every other lookup falls through to the node-type dictionary.",
    "sld_companion": "Optional per-entry boolean. When true, the entry is an ADDITIONAL family placed alongside whatever the (node_type, variant) lookup resolves — loaded into the resolver's companion collection, never the node-type dictionary (last-wins there would clobber the primary). One live use: L1-1 GFP places the GFI box (primary) plus a Circuit-Breaker/CB glyph (companion). Companion instances are counted and reported separately from devices and are invisible to compare_placement's geometry join (their placement-CSV kind is 'companion').",
    "sld_node_name": "Human-readable name from the Symbol Registry, provided for cross-reference verification.",
    "coverage_summary": {
      "mapped": 20,
      "placeholder_family_exists": 3,
      "no_family": 11,
      "generic_linework": 1,
      "total_sld_nodes": 35
    },
    "variant_selectors": "Root table: sld_node_type \u2192 dotted path naming WHERE on the topology object the variant value is read from (e.g. 'data_fields.kind'). Putting the discriminator's source path in the contract rather than in C# keeps the resolver generic \u2014 variant-ising a second node type later is a pure data change with no recompile. Semantics: dotted path, stringified, trimmed, matched case-insensitively; a missing or unmatched value falls back to the node_type-only entry."
  },
